*> PLB-C094 open-after-lock: an OPEN of a file closed WITH LOCK.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LOCKED.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "out.dat" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT LOG-FILE ASSIGN TO "log.dat" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  OUT-FILE.
01  OUT-REC             PIC X(10).
FD  LOG-FILE.
01  LOG-REC             PIC X(10).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FS               PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    *> Reported: in the same list, and in the next sentence.
    OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE
    CLOSE OUT-FILE WITH LOCK
    OPEN INPUT OUT-FILE
    CLOSE OUT-FILE LOCK.
    OPEN EXTEND OUT-FILE.
    *> Not reported: CLOSE without LOCK; the lock of another file in
    *> the same CLOSE; a GO TO between.
    OPEN OUTPUT LOG-FILE
    CLOSE LOG-FILE
    OPEN INPUT LOG-FILE
    CLOSE OUT-FILE WITH LOCK LOG-FILE
    OPEN OUTPUT LOG-FILE
    IF WS-FS = "00"
        CLOSE LOG-FILE WITH LOCK
        GO TO FINISH
    END-IF
    OPEN INPUT LOG-FILE.
FINISH.
    CLOSE LOG-FILE
    STOP RUN.
